@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+## Missing context
+
+- Task 1's `crates/features/show/src/tasks.rs` builds each task block from `header()` and `footer()` only. It never calls `runs` or `events`, so there is no place where this task can add the run lines between a task's `Verify:` line and its `Scope:` line.
+- `crates/features/show/src/text.rs` only appends `runs::LINES` after `archived::LAND` and before `digest::LINES`. Any line `runs.rs` returns therefore lands at the end of the change text, not inside the `Tasks:` section the goldens require.
+- `events::section` is called after `tasks::section`, so it can print the `Event Timeline:` section but cannot insert lines into an already-built `Tasks:` section.
+
+## Blocked
+
+The task's premise is false: the acceptance says "`src/text.rs`, `src/tasks.rs` and the other sections already call both modules", but `tasks.rs` calls neither. The goldens put each task's run lines between `Verify:` and `Scope:`, and "Show run history" requires the whole output of `approved`, `003` and `004-dead` to equal its golden. With only `events.rs`, `events/**`, `runs.rs`, `runs/**` and `tests/show_runs.rs` in scope there is no integration point that can move run lines into the `Tasks:` section.
+
+I need `crates/features/show/src/tasks.rs` added to this task's scope so `task_lines` can call a `runs` function for the event-derived lines (or task 1's scaffold fixed to call it). `crates/features/show/src/text.rs` should also be in scope, at least to stop appending `runs::LINES` after the land section, unless that constant is left empty and `runs` exposes a per-task function instead. The `Event Timeline:` half needs no scope change.
+
+## Next
+
+After the scope is amended, implement the `Tasks:` run lines in `runs.rs` and wire them from `tasks.rs`, then prove `Covers: rust-show/show-run-history`.
+
+Touched:
